# Security Rules (details in @docs/SECURITY.md)

- Passwords: `argon2` (or bcrypt cost ≥ 12). Never log or return hashes.
- JWT: access 15m, refresh 7d, refresh tokens stored hashed and rotated; revoke on logout.
- All routes protected by default (global `JwtAuthGuard`); public ones use `@Public()`.
- RBAC via `@Roles()`: `USER`, `ADMIN`. Check ownership: a user only accesses own bookings.
- Validate ALL input with DTOs; whitelist enabled. Validate UUID params with `ParseUUIDPipe`.
- Secrets only via env; `.env` never committed; validate env at boot.
- Rate limit with `@nestjs/throttler`: strict on `/auth/*`, booking and payment endpoints.
- Helmet + CORS allowlist. No stack traces in responses.
- Payment webhooks: verify signature, reject replays, process idempotently. Never trust client-sent amount; compute server-side from show price.
- Don't log PII, tokens, card data, or full request bodies.
- Parameterized queries only.
